[10:03:24] ADDRESSED_RESPONSES
RESPONSE_TO CC2 | In Round 0, I predicted that calculating gamma strictly on the novel finding subset (excluding the 58.3% churn) would yield a gamma of ~0.45-0.55. The raw Duane gamma is too sticky due to early cumulative mass to cross 0.5 quickly, but a novel-only gamma isolates the true architecture convergence signal.
RESPONSE_TO DeepSeek | Confirmed. A mandatory, structured CHALLENGE mechanism directly absorbs the disagreement load, allowing models to explicitly resolve edge cases without the automated immune system registering it as false-positive 'noise' and triggering autoimmune lockouts.

VERDICTS
CONFIRM Codex_F003
CONFIRM Codex_F006
CONFIRM ChatGPT_F002
CHALLENGE DeepSeek_D002R1 | evidence: A 43% character reduction assumes all eliminated churn tokens translate to pure savings without any replacement by novel analysis. The 22-30% range estimated by Codex_F007 and ChatGPT_F004 aligns better with baseline verbosity constraints and historical model behavior.
EXTEND ChatGPT_F005 | A 3-model vs 5-model ablation test must also measure wall-clock review time per round, as parallelization across 5 models might reach coverage in fewer rounds than 3 models, addressing the strict PoC time-to-completion constraint.

