  "EVIDENCE": "Exp 31: 150 cross-model references, zero CHALLENGEs. kappa=0.619 shows substantial agreement — models agreed on what was wrong. But without formal disagreement or closure, the finding space is monotonically non-decreasing. Every round adds findings; none are ever removed. This is structurally incompatible with gamma > 0.5.",
  "FOLLOW": "Protocol format (SVP-2) provides the CHALLENGE verb but does not guarantee models will use it. The closure protocol (STATUS lines + confirmation) provides an alternative path: findings close by resolution rather than disagreement. Prediction: in Exp 33, CHALLENGEs will remain rare (<5% of verdicts) because models genuinely tend to agree. Closure via STATUS+CONFIRM will be the primary contraction mechanism. Falsifiable: if Exp 33 still shows zero CHALLENGEs AND zero closures after 5 rounds, the closure protocol has failed and a harder mechanism is needed (e.g., forced adversarial assignment).",
  "CONCLUSION": "The closure protocol is the critical addition to SVP-2. Without it, no protocol format change will produce convergence. CHALLENGE frequency is a secondary indicator — closure rate is primary.",
  "CONFIDENCE": 0.85
}
