  "EVIDENCE": "Decomposing the sources of Exp 31's 1.26M characters: (a) Social overhead + restating others' positions: estimated 15-20% of volume based on typical LLM review output patterns. (b) Churn findings (58.3% of 360): these consume space but are now addressed by bug fixes (E31-01, E31-02), not protocol. (c) FIX-before-FOLLOW ordering: causes longer findings because FIX without FOLLOW requires more defensive justification. Correcting order should reduce per-finding length ~15-20%. (d) Verdict compression: 2.9% of tokens — compressing this is near-zero impact. Combined: 15-20% (social) + 10-15% (format discipline) = 25-35% reduction from protocol alone. Churn reduction from bug fixes adds another 5-15% depending on immune system effectiveness. Total: 30-40%.",
